# The GIS engine for the Python worker (describe_dataset, query_features,
# vector_op, verify, raster_op). The worker's protocol, SQL reads and plugin host need
# only the standard library; these add GDAL-backed reading and writing,
# geometry and coordinate systems. All publish wheels for Windows, macOS and
# Linux that bundle GDAL and PROJ, so no separate GDAL install is needed.
#
# This is the source: requirements-gis.txt is generated from it, pinned by
# exact version and by the SHA-256 of every file, for Windows x64, macOS
# arm64 and Linux x64 on CPython 3.12 and 3.13. Edit this file, then run
#   python packaging/engine/compile-requirements.py
# and install the .txt with --require-hashes (never this file).
geopandas>=1.0,<2
pyogrio>=0.10,<1
# 2.1 or later: line geometries with M values (T-19).
shapely>=2.1,<3
pyproj>=3.6,<4
pandas>=2.2,<4
